    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The Aghlabid conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> began with a landing at Mazara del Vallo in 827 and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palermo">Palermo</a> in 831, but the island was not fully conquered until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taormina">Taormina</a> fell in 902.</li><li>From 948 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalbid-dynasty">Kalbid dynasty</a> ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> as autonomous <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">emirs</a> while formally acknowledging the Fatimid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphs</a>.</li><li>Arab rule brought land reforms, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qanat">qanat</a> irrigation and new crops such as oranges, lemons, pistachio and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugarcane">sugarcane</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-hawqal">Ibn Hawqal</a>, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> merchant who visited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palermo">Palermo</a> in 950, reckoned 7,000 butchers trading in 150 shops in the city.</p></aside>
    </section>

